# libdom: node.compareDocumentPosition implemented (patch 508)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 507)
#
# _dom_node_compare_document_position returned DOM_NOT_SUPPORTED_ERR. It
# is the DOM spec's tree-order comparison now, over the parent and sibling
# pointers: lift the deeper node to the other's depth (an ancestor or a
# descendant is CONTAINS|PRECEDING / CONTAINED_BY|FOLLOWING), climb both to
# the children of the common ancestor, and walk siblings out from one in
# both directions until the other is met. Nodes in different trees are
# DISCONNECTED | IMPLEMENTATION_SPECIFIC with a consistent PRECEDING /
# FOLLOWING (by address), as the spec allows.
#
# Used by the bridge's native Node.prototype.compareDocumentPosition
# (508-netsurf-native-compare-document-position.patch).
--- a/src/core/node.c
+++ b/src/core/node.c
@@ -1425,17 +1425,89 @@
